  <section data-label="Lab B1: cache &amp; route" class="slide light cat-themed" style="--c: #16a34a;">
    <div class="glow soft"></div>
    <div class="frame">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="num">36</span>Lab B1</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Cache the review prompt and <span class="accent">route to a cheaper model</span>.</h2>

      <div class="frame-body">
      <div class="lab" style="margin-top: 20px; --c: #16a34a;">
        <span class="lab-tag">Lab B1: cache + route, measure savings</span>
        <h3>Build a PR-review call over token-efficient-workshop-node</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 23px; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 14px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> cache the stable review prompt prefix and route to a mid-tier model; measure the input-cost drop against your Lab 0 baseline.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Write a script that sends a PR diff from <code>token-efficient-workshop-node</code> to the API with a fixed system prompt (TypeScript review rules + 20 examples). Record baseline input tokens and cost without caching.</li>
          <li>Add <code>cache_control: {type: "ephemeral"}</code> to the system prompt block (the stable prefix). Re-run and confirm <code>usage.cache_read_input_tokens</code> is non-zero on the second call.</li>
          <li>Switch the model from top tier (Opus 4.8) to mid tier (Sonnet 4.6). Compare output quality and total cost.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="lab-out"><strong>Expected result:</strong> a large drop in input cost from caching (up to 90% on repeated calls) and a further cost reduction from model routing, with similar review quality. Record all three numbers: baseline, cached, cached + routed.</p>
      </div>      </div>
    </div>
